WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.220 --> 00:00:03.220
Film Courage: Why do you write?

00:00:03.220 --> 00:00:06.109
Josh Healey, Writer/Producer/Comedian - The
North Pole Show: Why do I write?

00:00:06.109 --> 00:00:10.560
Ooohhh…you’re asking the big questions.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:20.779
I write because I think otherwise I would
go crazy (or crazier than I already am).

00:00:20.779 --> 00:00:22.259
Film Courage: It’s a good crazy.

00:00:22.259 --> 00:00:24.699
Josh: Yes, it’s a good crazy (mostly).

00:00:24.699 --> 00:00:34.790
Writing is a beautiful and also masochistic
sport that like I love writing but it’s…it’s…let’s

00:00:34.790 --> 00:00:40.330
talk about the good stuff.

00:00:40.330 --> 00:00:43.800
I mean I write because I’ve got something
to say.

00:00:43.800 --> 00:00:51.310
I write because there are things that I want
to see that are different in the world.

00:00:51.310 --> 00:00:56.430
There’s things, there are characters, there’s
people that I know and love whose stories

00:00:56.430 --> 00:01:02.790
deserve to be told, whose aren’t told in
the mainstream media or Hollywood or even

00:01:02.790 --> 00:01:03.790
just the local press.

00:01:03.790 --> 00:01:09.381
It’s like whose story is told, how is it
told, who are the heroes and s-heroes, who

00:01:09.381 --> 00:01:10.820
are the villains.

00:01:10.820 --> 00:01:15.580
I just don’t feel…I want to complicate
the narrative.

00:01:15.580 --> 00:01:23.560
I want to show a different perspective and
I also want to have some fun.

00:01:23.560 --> 00:01:31.920
So for me writing is the way to be both as
serious or as ridiculous as I am on a given

00:01:31.920 --> 00:01:33.350
day.

00:01:33.350 --> 00:01:43.030
And I want to show the breadth of who we are
as people and I want to show you know there’s

00:01:43.030 --> 00:01:51.460
a quote by one of my heroes Bertolt Brecht,
an old German, socialist, playwright and poet

00:01:51.460 --> 00:01:58.150
and he said “Art is not a mirror to hold
up to society but a hammer with which to shape

00:01:58.150 --> 00:01:59.150
it.”

00:01:59.150 --> 00:02:05.990
And so for me writing, filmmaking (all of
these things) are a way to not just provoke

00:02:05.990 --> 00:02:11.120
people’s ideas but to show a different idea
of what is possible.

00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:19.290
And in this country where we are so isolated
or so individualistic, we’re so divided

00:02:19.290 --> 00:02:28.940
and put up against each other where all of
the struggles of American government, political

00:02:28.940 --> 00:02:37.480
corruption, racism (go down the list) let’s
use art to show something different.

00:02:37.480 --> 00:02:43.550
And not to ignore the pain put to name the
reality of this, these are the problems that

00:02:43.550 --> 00:02:50.770
are affecting people’s daily lives, but
what could it look like if it was something

00:02:50.770 --> 00:02:51.770
a little different.

00:02:51.770 --> 00:02:55.160
So art and writing is about that radical imagination.

00:02:55.160 --> 00:03:01.050
Film Courage: Have you ever written something
whether it’s performance [spoken word] or

00:03:01.050 --> 00:03:05.250
a screenplay that it bothered someone and
they were very angry about it?

00:03:05.250 --> 00:03:06.370
Josh: Oh hell yeah!

00:03:06.370 --> 00:03:08.420
Film Courage: How does this make you feel?

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:15.120
Josh: It feels like I’m doing my job.

00:03:15.120 --> 00:03:21.450
One of the main criteria…one of the main
signs of feedback that I’m doing my job

00:03:21.450 --> 00:03:26.400
right is the level of angry emails that I
get.

00:03:26.400 --> 00:03:31.230
If I’m not pissing someone off, I’m not
doing my job as a writer.

00:03:31.230 --> 00:03:39.960
If I’m not making you…if I’m not challenging
you…you know I want my art to afflict the

00:03:39.960 --> 00:03:42.940
comfortable and comfort the afflicted.

00:03:42.940 --> 00:03:50.930
So if people in power are tapping me on my
back (if I just have “yes-men” as you

00:03:50.930 --> 00:03:54.959
said) like “Oh, that’s good” then I
could just be making soda pop commercials

00:03:54.959 --> 00:03:58.840
but that’s not what I want to be doing.

00:03:58.840 --> 00:04:06.790
Yes, there are times…I’m a Jewish writer
who writes about Israel and Palestine sometimes.

00:04:06.790 --> 00:04:08.470
I can be a little controversial.

00:04:08.470 --> 00:04:12.500
I’m a white guy who talks about race and
white privilege.

00:04:12.500 --> 00:04:15.400
Yeah…sometimes people have some feelings
about that.

00:04:15.400 --> 00:04:19.579
I work with a multi-racial team of writers
in Oakland [San Francisco Bay Area], even

00:04:19.579 --> 00:04:23.330
in the writer’s room we challenge each other.

00:04:23.330 --> 00:04:28.330
Sometimes we’re not sure if they’re saying
what they want to say.

00:04:28.330 --> 00:04:30.880
Am I speaking on behalf of someone else?

00:04:30.880 --> 00:04:37.320
Are you saying what is a real representation
or is that a stereotype?

00:04:37.320 --> 00:04:44.211
So the first thing I feel like is in the writer’s
room is even before the writer’s room, am

00:04:44.211 --> 00:04:45.470
I challenging myself?

00:04:45.470 --> 00:04:52.930
If I’m not challenged or I’m not surprised
or if I’m not in a new place by the end

00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:56.389
of the writing by the end of the writing that
I was at the start then I haven’t done my

00:04:56.389 --> 00:04:58.919
own job to myself.

00:04:58.919 --> 00:05:05.560
And so I feel like that’s…you’ve got
to end somewhere new.

00:05:05.560 --> 00:05:10.370
Film Courage: Has anyone ever said can you
tone it down?

00:05:10.370 --> 00:05:12.850
What is your response to this?

00:05:12.850 --> 00:05:20.630
Josh: Um…you know that great classic movie
THIS IS SPINAL TAP?

00:05:20.630 --> 00:05:23.910
I turn it to 11.

00:05:23.910 --> 00:05:25.200
We turn it up.

00:05:25.200 --> 00:05:27.750
We don’t have time to tone it down.

00:05:27.750 --> 00:05:30.530
There’s too much false politeness.

00:05:30.530 --> 00:05:39.420
There’s too much trying to make everyone…it’s
not that I want to stir controversy for the

00:05:39.420 --> 00:05:43.960
sake of controversy.

00:05:43.960 --> 00:05:51.650
I don’t want just to offend you or upset
you for the sake of reaction.

00:05:51.650 --> 00:05:55.620
The idea is can we look at some new perspectives?

00:05:55.620 --> 00:06:08.300
The idea is no matter where you stand we all
know that there are some things that are

00:06:08.300 --> 00:06:11.370
wiped between the rug (wiped under the rug).

00:06:11.370 --> 00:06:19.550
There are some things that are not talked
about that need to be talked about.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:23.990
If art and film and writing isn’t the place,
then where is the place to do that?

